{"name":"Soul Side","hex":"#ffaa55","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soul","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The spirit or essence of a person usually thought to consist of one's thoughts and personality, often believed to live on after the person's death.","The spirit or essence of anything."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characteristic of or pertaining to African American culture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soul"},{"term":"side","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bounding straight edge of a two-dimensional shape.","A flat surface of a three-dimensional object; a face."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Being on the left or right, or toward the left or right; lateral.","Indirect; oblique; incidental."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/side"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soul","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and philosophy, the soul is the immaterial aspect or essence of a living being. It is typically believed to be immortal and to exist apart from the material world. Anthropologists and psychologists have found that most humans believe in the existence of a soul or spirit, and that they have cross-culturally distinguished between the soul and the material body."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Schiavonetti_Soul_leaving_body_1808.jpg/330px-Schiavonetti_Soul_leaving_body_1808.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soul","wikidata":"Q9165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Schiavonetti_Soul_leaving_body_1808.jpg/500px-Schiavonetti_Soul_leaving_body_1808.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Schiavonetti_Soul_leaving_body_1808.jpg/1280px-Schiavonetti_Soul_leaving_body_1808.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con